ss MVC vs 24.9% of PGY1s, AOR 1.29 (95% CI 1.10–1.51); and 6.0% reported MVCs vs 4.2% of PGY1s, AOR 1.48 (95% CI 1.09–2.03)]. However, there were no statistically significant differences between the likelihood of self-reported hazardous driving events between PGY5 and PGY1 residents ( Table 3 ). TABLE 3. Adjusted Associations Between Resident and Program Characteristics and Hazardous Driving Events § Characteristic Adjusted ∥ Odds Ratios (95% Confidence Interval) Nodded Off While Driving or Stopped in Traffic Near-miss Motor Vehicle Crash ¶ Motor Vehicle Crash Sex Male 1.00 (REF) 1.00 (REF) 1.00 (REF) Female 1.08 (0.97–1.20) 1.20 (1.07–1.35) † 1.21 (0.97–1.50) Postgraduate year 1 1.00 (REF) 1.00 (REF) 1.00 (REF) 2 1.44 (1.24–1.67) ‡ 1.29 (1.10–1.51) † 1.48 (1.09–2.03) * 3 1.41 (1.20–1.64) ‡ 1.29 (1.09–1.52) † 1.53 (1.10–2.11) * 4 1.61 (1.38–1.89) ‡ 1.28 (1.08–1.52) † 1.48 (1.06–2.08) * 5 1.17 (0.99–1.39) 1.03 (0.86–1.24) 1.03 (0.70–1.52) Worked >28 h continuously # 0–2 times 1.00 (REF) 1.00 (REF) 1.00 (REF) 3 or more times 1.63 (1.39–1.91) ‡ 1.63 (1.39–1.93) ‡ 1.15 (0.86–1.54) Had <8 h off between shifts # 0–2 times 1.00 (REF) 1.00 (REF) 1.00 (REF) 3 or more times 1.24 (1.03–1.48) * 1.20 (1.00–1.44) 1.74 (1.28–2.35) ‡ Number of months exceeded 80-h per week rule over the past 6 mo (this academic year) 0 1.00 (REF) 1.00 (REF) 1.00 (REF) 1–2 1.82 (1.61–2.06) ‡ 1.82 (1.59–2.08) ‡ 1.15 (0.87–1.52) 3–4 2.23 (1.84–2.71) ‡ 2.44 (2.00–2.98) ‡ 2.21 (1.58–3.11) ‡ 5 or more 2.86 (2.21–3.69) ‡ 3.28 (2.53–4.24) ‡ 2.46 (1.65–3.67) ‡ GHQ-12 score 0–3 1.00 (REF) 1.00 (REF) 1.00 (REF) 4–12 1.48 (1.33–1.65) ‡ 1.96 (1.75–2.20) ‡ 2.55 (2.00–3.24) ‡ Program geographic region Northeast 1.00 (REF) 1.00 (REF) 1.00 (REF) Southeast 1.05 (0.83–1.32) 0.98 (0.77–1.24) 0.80 (0.55–1.16) Midwest 1.11 (0.89–1.38) 1.04 (0.83–1.31) 0.93 (0.66–1.31) Southwest 1.00 (0.75–1.33) 1.06 (0.79–1.42) 0.91 (0.59–1.42) West 1.23 (0.95–1.59) 1.26 (0.96–1.64) 0.82 (0.55–1.24) Primary program locale ** City 1.00 (