INSERT INTO corpus VALUES(1939,'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2448619','Surgical training posts in Northern Ireland: assessment by surgeons in training.','Thompson RL, Rowlands BJ, Johnston GW, Parks TG, Irwin ST.','1991','burnand mastership dehn blacklay diggory damned logie','Abstract Northern Ireland has one of the largest surgical training programmes in the United Kingdom. The surgical trainees'' assessment of the quality of training provided has been collated prospectively since 1983, and provides a useful insight into the strengths and weaknesses of the programme, as well as the training value of individual posts. The overall quality of clinical training in surgery was considered to be well above average, but some registrars felt that supervision of operative surgery could be improved. Clinical research was considered to be of average quality in the teaching hospitals but below average in district general hospitals. In the current climate of restriction of the number of training posts in general surgery, the views of the trainees should not be neglected in assessing which posts are best suited for training. Full text PDF Previous 75 76 77 78 79 Next Selected References These references are in PubMed. This may not be the complete list of references from this article. Burnand K. G., Young A. E. What price the mastership of surgery? Lancet. 1984 May 19;1(8386):1114–1115. doi: 10.1016/s0140-6736(84)92521-2. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Dehn T. C., Blacklay P. F., Taylor G. W. A survey of registrars undertaking general surgical research in the United Kingdom on 1 October 1983. Br J Surg. 1985 Aug;72(8):668–671. doi: 10.1002/bjs.1800720829. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Diggory R. T. Training of surgical registrars: a regional audit. BMJ. 1988 Aug 13;297(6646):455–456. doi: 10.1136/bmj.297.6646.455-a. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Irwin S. T., Roy A. D. Publish or be damned! Lancet. 1984 Oct 13;2(8407):859–859. doi: 10.1016/s0140-6736(84)90887-0. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Ritchie W. P., Jr, Cohn L. H. Surgical residencies reviewed by surgical residents. An analysis of American general surgical training programs by the trainees. Surgery. 1980 Aug;88(2):315–325. [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Steele R. J., Logie J. R., Munro A. Technical training in surgery: the trainee''s view. Br J Surg. 1989 Dec;76(12):1291–1293. doi: 10.1002/bjs.1800761222. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ]',3,'2025-10-13 08:39:05','2025-10-13 08:39:05');
